From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] AMLAudioTrim: hold the audio clock in step with the master
 clock

Add CAMLAudioTrim, a rate loop that trims mpll0 so the passthrough audio
clock holds against the master clock, fed from the latency measurement and
armed by the audio-lead setting.

Aim it at the residual offset, pick the trim node by SoC (including S7D and
S6), and leave the integrator alone when the setting is Off: hold m_want at
rest and reset m_clamped, so the watchdog cannot latch a stand-down while
nothing is being written. The branch sits after the median and plausibility
test, so the measurement is unchanged, and a genuine stand-down still latches.

Signed-off-by: allolive <160342668+allolive@users.noreply.github.com>

